            <ArticleTitle>[Lesions of the coronary bed in patients with ischemic heart disease and ECG changes at rest].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The data of ECG at rest and of coronary angiography have been analyzed in 184 patients. Correlations between various ECG changes and the coronary bed involvement have been revealed. The authors have calculated the sensitivities and specificities of some ECG symptoms for the prediction of an atherosclerotic involvement of the coronary arteries. A sufficiently high specificity of ECG examination (89.1%) makes it useful for active detection of coronary patients, whereas its low specificity (54.2%) necessitates employment of supplementary methods of investigation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
